{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/javascript/angular-standalone-components/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"title":"Labidi Aymen"}},"markdownRemark":{"id":"8d13a886-765b-51b8-bc8b-2ce1971e5662","excerpt":"At ReactConfg 2018 Event, Dan Abramov explained the Logo of React, he said that the user interface can be splitted into small independent units called…","html":"<h2></h2>\n<p>At ReactConfg 2018 Event, Dan Abramov explained the Logo of React, he said that the user interface can be splitted into small independent units called components - similar to an Atom - and they will focus, in the next few years, on Hooks: “Electrons” as he named them.</p>\n<p>On the other side of the Javascript world, Angular started focusing on smaller units as Component, Directive and Pipes rather than modules.</p>\n<p>Starting from Angular 14, Components can be standalone and imported into modules or other components without the need for a dedicated module.</p>\n<h2>Standalone Component in Action.</h2>\n<p>To test this feature, I created a blank project and activated the routing option.</p>\n<p>Then, I created a basic component <code class=\"language-text\">UserDetailComponent </code> , the metadata looks like the following.</p>\n<p><div id=\"gist116763322\" class=\"gist\">\n    <div class=\"gist-file\" translate=\"no\" data-color-mode=\"light\" data-light-theme=\"light\">\n      <div class=\"gist-data\">\n        \n<div class=\"js-gist-file-update-container js-task-list-container\">\n      <div id=\"file-standalone-component-ts\" class=\"file my-2\">\n    \n    <div itemprop=\"text\"\n      class=\"Box-body p-0 blob-wrapper data type-typescript  \"\n      style=\"overflow: auto\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\"\n      aria-label=\"standalone-component.ts content, created by labidiaymen on 10:00AM on June 10, 2022.\"\n    >\n\n        \n<div class=\"js-check-hidden-unicode js-blob-code-container blob-code-content\">\n\n  <template class=\"js-